# What a deployment does not need.
#
# Only relevant to `vercel` from a terminal, which uploads the working directory rather than cloning
# the repo. Without this it would ship node_modules and a previous build, which on a project
# carrying 46MB of demo footage is the difference between an upload that finishes and one that
# looks hung.
#
# Everything the build genuinely needs stays: `demo/` is read by the prebuild seed step, and
# `public/seed/` is the footage the deployed pages play.
node_modules
.next
.data
.git
docs
tests
.claude
*.log
